lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n The rms value of emf induced in the coil if B varies harmonically at a frequency of 1 kHz</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 14 kV</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 18 kV</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 22 kV</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 28 kV</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (b)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/7e45ed45d1c2758c0b37d96b4c262287d9252075.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":18,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n If the area of outer and inner two concentric spheres be <em>A<sub>a</sub></em> and <em>A<sub>b</sub></em> respectively and the dielectric between two spheres being air, then the capacity of a spherical condenser (capacitor) is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/df00ee89f10f8bc547d93c2d21fe4863b17132c2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/4eab27731243d097ddb96759eef4b4c988e8db90.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/0332f9f88ac5025462d4332743addbb5b3af77f3.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/6b0037299dca78cff71f18acd438b7c87de56cd2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (b)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/06928fdb1bd6fe3d3777adac9f6b847632c345e4.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":19,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n Two current loops parallel to each other having radius of 0.12 m both carries current of 150 A in the same direction. Axis of the loops is along z-axis. One loop is at z = 0 m and another loop is at z = 0.25 m. The magnetic flux density <em>B</em> at a point midway between the loops is ________ mT. (Answer upto two decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0.45","high":"0.6"},"solution":"<p>\n 0.52 (0.45 - 0.60)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/9134b55b7b26e700b3609ed44e4db57f48c0ca2b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":20,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n An electromagnet is made of a ferromagnetic material whose magnetization curve can be approximated by</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/dcb5052110931614b5343d83a8c3d49c3a727084.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n If <em>H</em> = 250 A/m, then μ<em><sub>r</sub></em> is _______</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"4.3","high":"4.7"},"solution":"<p>\n 4.54 (4.30 - 4.70)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/c35ee301af22b3d9ee5801960a9ed349e2f4fd7c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":21,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n The magnetic field intensity <img src=\"/media/823d025dc14457ed86b8cd38fcd42690c70854a4.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> at the center of the current carrying circular loop shown in the figure is</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/71e4487ee52e225afc3487d167984c298d600fc8.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/681acc6b7aacd136213fd724cc5cbf77716d4226.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/280facde33ffa5c61c8ce9d83a244ec4eac6bfe3.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/7282e509c37ffebc3ba5b79b5c1b36f029b09d61.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/3e78cef87fea10d65912f83bf0d0b9a8a3e260ef.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (d)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/8b584a870aab23f8c319ecfd618a030ec234f511.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":22,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider a straight conductor of length 2 m. Carrying a current of 10 A in the +z direction. If the conductor is placed in a field of <img src=\"/media/2cf0ac00ddd0f4706d245acb5dc92969c76ba240.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> then the force on per unit length of the conductor is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/ad3238e11a7e933eeced7aad7475932291b0fadc.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/1524d7f9ab3c980c179d8ebb3491f78689f4024e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/bc4585f34ab185d1d7406efab5521e75d474021c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/2444201ce7d8ae4d280f6eb3900b6be8a0ca6863.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (c)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/4723cb0d80abe445ded1cfbcd37ae328b9cb9519.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":23,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n A vector <img src=\"/media/4c21a7c877eda873cf7baafed183d2ada4cdb8a6.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> Which of the following statements is TRUE?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/afbd2316f5f783ea1ef5cbaf5b4fa2f5737bf491.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> is solenoidal, but not irrotational</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/afbd2316f5f783ea1ef5cbaf5b4fa2f5737bf491.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> is irrotational, but not solensoidal</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/afbd2316f5f783ea1ef5cbaf5b4fa2f5737bf491.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> is neither solenoidal nor irrotational</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/afbd2316f5f783ea1ef5cbaf5b4fa2f5737bf491.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" />is both solenoidal and irrotational</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (a)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/9f44f3e764589e0e1a18d7edee50887d38a34cf5.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":24,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n Two identical conducting spheres <em>A</em> and <em>B</em> with negligible surface area have 3.1 nC and –0.1 nC charges on them respectively. They are brought into contact once and are then separated by a distance of 50 cm. The magnitude of force between them after separation is_________nN. (Answer upto two decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"80","high":"81.5"},"solution":"<p>\n 80.89 (80.00 - 81.50)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/d8d9d04387bcaaebeaa42cd55263d14eae9b4495.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":25,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n In a source free region in vaccum, if the electrostatic potential <img src=\"/media/fbf5cda28d72a86dde3d94e36420e6035cf14110.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> the value of constant c must be _______ .</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"-3","high":"-3"},"solution":"<p>\n -3</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/b92c4176e24da9c142c760bbb57cbe8eb7e60401.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":26,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n Two uniformly distributed line charges of <img src=\"/media/d4571ce552be92f98985b8bb24ff860655ffcd7c.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> = 5nc/m each are parallel to the <em>X</em>-axis, one at z = 0 and y = –2m and the other z = 0 and y = 4 m. The field <em>E</em> at (4, 1, 3) m is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/7f1dbd0f6bdef62dad2d619a98da5772a6c742d8.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/562f9fa4178f35c644a22b6ce28eefcc21064600.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/0ebc7e8e87016f5928466ad17aa15615bda82ffe.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/40edac05b2a49b54d663603d44ee61271d1dd188.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (d)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/ba97497d419d373ab1f4590f9830af2e2d24c9ef.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":27,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n The spherical surfaces with <em>R</em> = 1, 2 and 3 m carry surface charge densities of 20, –9 and 2 nC/m<sup>2 </sup>respectively. The electric flux leaving the surface at R = 5 m is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 12. 27 nC</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/2ec0aec78b369f71a2b8037257727929a165fbf6.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 14 nC</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/aeebd7cd85fc0daf0fbf71227ace86e1aa4d6ee7.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (b)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/ea085cdbda140126fd9b82028cd4c601dfe1a22e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/eda15627aaaf54652c356e6104329f9f434bb971.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":28,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n A circuit has 2000 turns enclosing a magnetic circuit 30 cm2 in section. A current of 5 A in the circuit produces a field of flux density 1(Tesla) and when current is doubled, flux density increases only by 50%. The mean value of inductance of the circuit between 5 A and 10 A is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 0.4 H</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 0.5 H</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 0.6 H</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 0.7 H</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (c)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/f97966452193d419d5690c7f0bbfe3d2f1ad0097.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":29,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n An electron (<em>q</em><sub>1</sub>) is moving in free space with velocity 10<sup>5</sup> m/s towards a stationary electron (<em>q</em><sub>2</sub>) far away. The closest distance that this moving electron gets to the stationary electron before the repulsive force diverts its path is _____ × 10<sup>–8</sup> m. (Answer upto two decimal places)<br />\n [Given, mass of electron <em>m</em> = 9.11 × 10<sup>–31</sup> kg, charge of electron <em>e</em> = – 1.6 × 10<sup>–19</sup>C, and permittivity ε<sub>0</sub> = <img src=\"/media/ea9495eb97fee030112aab5420cc70181b87a436.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> × 10<sup>–9</sup> F/m]</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"4.5","high":"5.5"},"solution":"<p>\n 5.05 (4.50 - 5.50)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/9f59ebd01a7d7ef65c58e4922a3f2a61bf764e8c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/83a3c5647722fd0d0d07cabc45642ff3f6c09dce.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":30,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n The parallel-plate capacitor shown in the figure has movable plates. The capacitor is charged so that the energy stored in it is <em>E</em> when the plate separation is <em>d</em>. The capacitor is then isolated electrically and the plates are moved such that the plate separation becomes 2<em>d</em>.</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/ec324513680bee460418d143b444aee35787c483.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n At this new plate separation, what is the energy stored in the capacitor, neglecting fringing effects?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n 2<em>E</em></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/53987aaaead41856845719308291a69110f6a6b9.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>E</em></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>E</em>/2</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (a)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/98380aa0ea76f84020006657bbd9da4a240a88aa.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":31,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n If the charge on each of the capacitors shown in figure is 4500 μC the voltage distribution across <em>C</em><sub>1</sub>, <em>C</em><sub>2</sub>, <em>C</em><sub>3</sub> is in the ratio 2 : 3 : 4 the total capacitance is</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/b7c28c1c8e32a1bab108d6c35771342d31b3e93c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 22.41 μF</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 42.51 μF</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 33.33 μF</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 39.26 μF</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (c)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/23d2c9c9f4a657082dc9ea65d5ab6f5da3c937c0.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":32,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n If <img src=\"/media/06ed86e78405b5a3731109665dde3a9b007071b2.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> = rsinθcosΦ, y = rsinθsinΦ, z = rcosθ, then</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/0b4e2cc2577848c574fbb517e17f09b5471ce12c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n The value of n is ________ .</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"2","high":"2"},"solution":"<p>\n 2</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/b898e8fb279646ab2bfcc4741cdb1369b32cba0d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/322152c5b6e91ac887e24e2d795fdedbe7f93f06.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":33,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n A uniformly distributed line charge with linear charge density <img src=\"/media/7af82c6fa7777efe96f91a084d1a18e920374ba5.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> = –4 nC/m is located at z = –4 m and <em>y</em> = 3 m. Similarly a uniform sheet charge with surface charge density σ = –0.2 nC/m<sup>2</sup> is positioned at z = 4 m. The magnitude of resultant electric field, <em>E</em> at point <em>P</em>(a, – 2, 0)m, will be ________ . (Answer upto two decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"9.5","high":"10"},"solution":"<p>\n 9.77 (9.50 - 10.00)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/9ba997926b98062f692d8ef4bcb7471d59894cff.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/879cf4b31f5b190bcac40036a8bd7a098ce9e995.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"}],"questionCount":33,"parsedAt":"2026-11-10T19:39:11.094Z"}